course: dictionary
lesson: 11770
title: Words about volcanoes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from a smaller word. Basaltic comes from basalt, the name of a dark, heavy rock. When you see the ending -ic, think "like" or "made of", so basaltic means made of basalt or like basalt.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The walkers climbed over the dark, basaltic rock by the sea.» The rock is dark and heavy, and the walkers are on the rock itself, so basaltic describes the rock. Swap in "made of basalt" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Science texts use basaltic a lot, and the other words near it are your clues. «The volcano poured out basaltic lava.» Lava is melted rock from a volcano, so basaltic lava is lava of this kind, and the word tells you the text is about volcanoes.
fact: Basalt is a dark, heavy rock.
fact: Basalt forms when lava from a volcano cools quickly.
fact: «Basaltic» means made of basalt, or like basalt or containing a lot of it.
fact: «Basaltic lava» is runny and can flow a long way, as in Hawaii and Iceland.
fact: Words ending in -ic often mean "like" or "made of", as in volcanic and basaltic.
exercise: «The walkers climbed over the dark, basaltic rock by the sea.» What does basaltic mean here? | Hot and bright like the sun | Wet and slippery like seaweed | Soft and white like chalk | *Made of basalt, a dark, heavy rock
exercise: «The volcano poured out basaltic lava, and it flowed for miles.» What is basaltic lava? | Lava that is thick and stops at once | *Lava that is runny and flows a long way | Lava that is cold, like snow | Lava that is bright blue
exercise: Ben says, «Basaltic just means dark.» Why is that not quite right? | Basaltic means hot and bubbling | *Basalt is a rock, and basaltic means made of it or like it | Basaltic means shiny and smooth | Basaltic means a kind of cloud
test: «The lava cooled quickly and became basalt.» What is basalt? | A light, floaty rock | A type of cloud | A kind of sand | *A dark, heavy rock
test: Which phrase uses basaltic correctly? | basaltic sunshine | basaltic music | *basaltic columns | basaltic bread
exam: «Scientists studied the basaltic rock from the sea floor and found it was dark and heavy.» What does basaltic describe? | The scientists | Hawaii | The weather | *The rock, which is made of basalt
